{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The line graph shows the distance that Andrew walked over time.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>How long did it take Andrew to walk the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf7fb728914bfacb3969daedced3ef8123d0cbdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 15 \\text{ minutes} \\\\ \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\text{ hour, } 15 \\text{ minutes} \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ 1 \\text{ hour, } 45 \\text{ minutes} \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ 2 \\text{ hours} \\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ 45 \\text{ minutes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"98\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the graph, we can see that each tick on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> axis represents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f47349f7514e9700b74e962efb1da4faec53070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\text{ hour}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"38\" />. This means that Andrew reaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km at about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab71ef6f666a4c25e8a61251c9061afc55cdaf1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\text{ 3}{4} \\text{ hours}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/7/a87e8c85cca0a4fdbeebcb5b6ed4f6a1203d4097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} \\times 60 = 45 \\text{ minutes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"38\" />, so this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33a4d359c6475a266432d6de66458d0210acc388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 1 \\text{ hour, } 45 \\text{ minutes}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"187\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the graph, we can see that Andrew reaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours but closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours. Of the answer choices, this best matches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33a4d359c6475a266432d6de66458d0210acc388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 1 \\text{ hour, } 45 \\text{ minutes}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"187\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" t